  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sameer Subhahs Mehata vs The State Of Maharashtra on 2 May, 2023 Author: Anuja Prabhudessai Bench: Anuja Prabhudessai P.H. Jayani 17 ABA1300.2023.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No. 1300 Of 2023 Mr. Sameer Subhash Mehata ... Applicant v/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Respondent Mr. Niranjan Mundargi i/b. Mr. S.V. Gavand, App for the State. Coram: Smt. Anuja Prabhudessai, J. Dated : 02nd May, 2023. P. C. :- .",
    "facts": "The aforesaid crime was registered pursuant to the FIR lodged by Umesh Subhash Bhuse, a Food Safety Officer. It is alleged that a vehicle which was carrying white substance was intercepted. It was revealed that the said substance is supplied by the Applicant to Shree Swami Samartha Milk Sameer Subhahs Mehata vs The State Of Maharashtra on 2 May, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/189653730/ 1 Collection for the purpose of adulteration of the milk. 4. The records reveal that the Applicant is a manufacturer of Melamine, a food addition substance. Learned APP states that there are no restrictions/guidelines as regards sale/purchase of the said substance. At this stage, there is no prima facie material to indicate that the Applicant had entered into criminal conspiracy and/or that the Applicant had supplied Melamine to the proprietor of Shree Swami Samarth Milk Collection for the purpose of adulteration of milk. In such circumstances, in my considered view, this is a fit case for interim bail. Learned APP states that pursuant to the said order, the Applicant has reported to the Investigating Officer and that he has been interrogated.",
    "arguments": "( c ) The Applicant shall not interfere with the complainant and the other witnesses and shall not tamper with the evidence or attempt to influence or contact the complainant, witnesses or any person concerned with the case in any manner ;",
